[10.8325, "o", "--- MAP ---\r\n"]
[10.833824, "o", "loomketch mill layout\r\n=====================\r\n\r\nketchcli/main.rs dispatches bind.\r\n\r\nOther crates sit beside ketchcli. Journals live in /app/vatlogs.\r\nFixture copies of those journals sit at /app/seed/vatlogs.\r\nbind refreshes /app/inkbay/bound.json, /app/inkbay/desk.tsv, and /app/inkbay/GUARD.\r\n\r\nbound.json uses object findings as a list of records\r\n{ \"issue\": N, \"kind\": \"<kind>\", \"frames\": [\"<sym>\", ...], \"body\": \"<text>\" }\r\nwhere issue is an integer that starts at 1. desk.tsv starts with header\r\nissue\tkind\tbody\r\nthen one tab-separated row per finding, using those same issue values.\r\n\r\nJournal text is AddressSanitizer form: one ERROR: kind line followed by #N frame lines.\r\nTemplate copy sits at /app/tplbay/bound.tpl.\r\nwalkcue/ holds an ops sidecar used when KETCH_ALPHA=1.\r\n\r\nA bind root such as /tmp/loom_out sits outside /app/vatlogs and must fail.\r\n\r\n"]
[10.834164, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@0b52e02d0353:/app# "]
[10.962989, "i", "echo '--- TREE ---'; find /app -maxdepth 3 -type f -printf '%p\\n' | sort; echo '--- BINARY ---'; file /app/bin/loomketch; head -c 16 /app/bin/loomketch | od -An -tx1\n"]
[10.963709, "o", "echo '--- TREE ---'; find /app -maxdepth 3 -type f -printf '%p\\n' | sort; echo '--- BINARY ---'; file /app/bin/loomketch; head -c 16 /app/bin/loomketch | od -An -tx1\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
